#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:-1
msgid ""
"A developer reference for the Spack Database format, describing its "
"structure, its compatibility across releases, how an index is converted with "
"spack reindex, and its version history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:13
msgid "Database Format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:15
msgid ""
"This document describes the Database format, which stores the specs "
"installed in an install tree as JSON, together with their prefix and whether "
"they were installed explicitly. The current version of the format is |"
"db_version|, defined by ``spack.database._DB_VERSION``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:18
msgid "An index in the Database format is found in the following places:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:20
msgid ""
"In ``<install_tree:root>/.spack-db/index.json``, for the install tree in use "
"and for each upstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:21
msgid ""
"In build caches, where the index lists the specs available in the build "
"cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:24
msgid "Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:26
msgid ""
"This section describes the current version of the format, |db_version|. An "
"index has a single top-level ``database`` key, which holds the version of "
"the format and one record for each spec:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:29
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"database\": {\n"
"    \"version\": \"9\",\n"
"    \"installs\": {\n"
"      \"nic37xsihlqze3xyg3xd6pthcgqxoy6p\": {\n"
"        \"spec\": {\n"
"          \"name\": \"zlib-ng\",\n"
"          \"version\": \"2.3.3\",\n"
"          \"dependencies\": [\n"
"            {\"name\": \"glibc\", \"hash\": "
"\"cyucshxqmd4krmsp7nco25trnybrdbam\", \"parameters\": {\"deptypes\": "
"[\"link\"], \"virtuals\": [\"libc\"]}}\n"
"          ],\n"
"          \"hash\": \"nic37xsihlqze3xyg3xd6pthcgqxoy6p\"\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"ref_count\": 0,\n"
"        \"path\": \"/opt/spack/linux-alderlake/zlib-ng-2.3.3-"
"nic37xsihlqze3xyg3xd6pthcgqxoy6p\",\n"
"        \"installed\": true,\n"
"        \"explicit\": true,\n"
"        \"installation_time\": 1759400000.0\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:54
msgid ""
"To keep the example short, most keys of ``spec`` and the remaining records "
"are not shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:56
msgid ""
"The version is a string. The records are keyed by DAG hash, and their order "
"is not significant. Besides the installed specs, the index has records for "
"specs that are not installed: dependencies that have no prefix, and "
"deprecated specs. Each record is a dictionary with the following keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:61
msgid "``spec``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:62
msgid ""
"The node dictionary of the spec, as described in :ref:`specfile-format`. "
"Each dependency is referred to by its DAG hash, and has a record of its own "
"in the same index, or in the index of an upstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:64
msgid "``ref_count``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:65
msgid ""
"The number of records that depend on this one, plus the number of records "
"deprecated in favor of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:66
msgid "``path``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:67
msgid "The installation prefix, or the prefix of an external."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:68
msgid "``installed``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:69
msgid "Whether the spec is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:70
msgid "``explicit``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:71
msgid "Whether the spec was installed explicitly, or only as a dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:72
msgid "``installation_time``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:73
msgid "The time of the installation, in seconds since the epoch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:74
msgid "``deprecated_for``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:75
msgid ""
"The DAG hash of the spec that replaces this one. It is present only in specs "
"deprecated with ``spack deprecate``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:77
msgid "``origin``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:78
msgid ""
"The value ``external-db``, for externals read from an external manifest. It "
"is not present in other records."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:81
msgid ""
"The index of a build cache has only the keys ``spec``, ``ref_count``, and "
"``in_buildcache`` in each record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:83
msgid ""
"A JSON schema of the format is in ``lib/spack/spack/schema/database_index."
"py``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:86
msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:88
msgid "An index in an older version is converted only by ``spack reindex``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:91
msgid ""
"Spack reads an index in an older version without modifying it, and commands "
"that would modify it fail with an error that requests ``spack reindex``. "
"After ``spack reindex``, the versions of Spack that wrote the previous index "
"can no longer read it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:94
msgid "The properties below are defined in :ref:`file-formats`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:96
msgid "**Backward compatibility**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:97
msgid ""
"An index in version 6 or later is read in place, so commands that only read "
"the Database, such as ``spack find``, work on it. An index in version 5 or "
"earlier is an error for every command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:100
msgid "**Forward compatibility**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:101
msgid "None. Reading a version newer than the current one is an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:104
msgid "**Rewrite policy**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:105
msgid ""
"An index in an older version is never rewritten implicitly. Commands that "
"modify the Database, such as ``spack install`` or ``spack uninstall``, check "
"the version before starting any work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:109
msgid "Converting an index with ``spack reindex``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:110
msgid ""
"``spack reindex`` writes a new index from the ``spec.json`` files of the "
"installation prefixes, and keeps a copy of the previous one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:112
msgid ""
"$ spack reindex\n"
"==> Created a backup copy of the DB at\n"
"  /opt/spack/.spack-db/index.json.bkp\n"
"==> The DB at /opt/spack/.spack-db/index.json has been reindexed to v9\n"
"  If you need to restore, replace it with the backup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:120
msgid ""
"If Spack can read the previous index, the values of ``explicit``, "
"``installation_time``, ``origin``, and ``deprecated_for`` are copied from "
"its records. Otherwise, every spec found in the install tree is recorded as "
"explicitly installed. Specs that are in the previous index and have no "
"prefix are kept, and are recorded as not installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:125
msgid "Upstreams and build caches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:126
msgid ""
"The index of an upstream is never written, so Spack cannot convert it. It is "
"read in place if it is in version 6 or later, and it is an error otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:129
msgid ""
"The index of a build cache follows the same rules when it is in an older "
"version. An index in a version newer than the current one is not used, and "
"Spack emits a warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:135
msgid "Version History"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:137
msgid ""
"The version is recorded in ``database.version``. Each version of the "
"Database is associated with one version of the spec file, which is used to "
"read the ``spec`` of every record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:140
msgid "**Version 9** *(Spack v1.3)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:141
msgid ""
"Records store spec file v6 nodes, which include the virtuals provided by "
"each node (`#53012 <https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/53012>`_). An index "
"in an older version is read in place, and writes to it are refused (`#53045 "
"<https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/53045>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:144
msgid "**Version 8** *(Spack v1.0)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:145
msgid ""
"Records store spec file v5 nodes, where compilers are build dependencies "
"(`#45189 <https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/45189>`_). An index in an "
"older version is an error for every command, including those that only read "
"the Database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:148
msgid "**Version 7** *(Spack v0.21)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:149
msgid ""
"Records store spec file v4 nodes, where virtuals are recorded on the edges "
"of the DAG (`#34821 <https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/34821>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:151
msgid "**Version 6** *(Spack v0.17)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:152
msgid ""
"Records store spec file v2 nodes (`#22845 <https://github.com/spack/spack/"
"pull/22845>`_). Spack v0.18 to v0.20 write the same version with spec file "
"v3 nodes, which have the same structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:155
msgid "**Version 5** *(Spack v0.13)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:156
msgid ""
"The version becomes an integer, and records can have the ``deprecated_for`` "
"key (`#13410 <https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/13410>`_). Records store "
"spec file v1 nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:159
msgid "**Versions 0.9 to 0.9.3** *(Spack v0.12 and earlier)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:160
msgid ""
"Version 0.9 is written by Spack v0.9, and version 0.9.2 by Spack v0.10. "
"Version 0.9.3, written by Spack v0.11 and v0.12, adds externals to the "
"Database (`#1167 <https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/1167>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/database.rst:163
msgid ""
"Up to Spack v0.23, an index in an older version was converted automatically: "
"it was either reindexed when read, or read and rewritten in the current "
"version on the next write."
msgstr ""
